  "rationale": "The Pareto front is well-established and feasible. We have identified a clear trade-off curve between power and accuracy. The minimum power design (pipelined_m, power_index=2.0) meets the throughput constraint (51.9 MSPS >= 50) and the accuracy constraint (12.8 bits > 12 bits). Higher accuracy designs (up to 14.04 bits) are also available at the cost of higher power (up to 4.85). The hypervolume is 75.19, indicating good coverage of the objective space. Since this is the final round, and the front covers the relevant range of the objectives (power 2-4.85, accuracy 12.8-14.0) with feasible designs at both ends, stopping is the appropriate action. The selection rule (min power_index) will pick the pipelined_m design with power_index=2.0."
